29o2|n|A species of asceticism among the Hindoos, which consists in a complete abstraction from all worldly objects, by which the votary expects to obtain union with the universal spirit, and to acquire superhuman faculties.	N:20g2,84,6;20hb,82,6;20z9,76,4~20hb,82,6;20g2,84,6;20z9,76,4
29pa|n|of Yourself	v:1mah,80,3~1mah,80,3	n:2nt,94,5;2ns,70,8~2ns,70,8;2nt,94,5
29pb|n|of Youth ; The quality or state of being young; youthfulness; juvenility. ; The part of life that succeeds to childhood; the period of existence preceding maturity or age; the whole early part of life, from childhood, or, sometimes, from infancy, to manhood. ; A young person; especially, a young man. ; Young persons, collectively.	N:vzb,58,4~vzb,58,4
29pc|a|Not yet mature or aged; young. ; Also used figuratively. ; Of or pertaining to the early part of life; suitable to early life; as, youthful days; youthful sports. ; Fresh; vigorous, as in youth.	j:omo,120,3~omo,120,3
